This package contains code copied (vendored) from two other MIT-licensed
packages. Since @seneca/mesh 2.0.0 it no longer depends on them. Both stay
on npm unchanged for the users of seneca-mesh 1.x.


1. swim (lib/swim/)

   Origin:   @voxgig/swim 0.7.0
             https://github.com/voxgig-attic/swim-js
             commit 9ddb2c664a95fc4e158e1eb386de8f0ecb6aaa08 (tag v0.7.0),
             identical to the npm tarball of @voxgig/swim 0.7.0.
             It is a fork of https://github.com/mrhooray/swim-js.
   Files:    lib/codec.js, lib/disseminator.js, lib/error.js,
             lib/failure-detector.js, lib/member.js, lib/membership.js,
             lib/message-type.js, lib/net.js and lib/swim.js of that commit,
             copied to lib/swim/ under the same names.
   Author:   Rui Hu <code@mrhooray.com> and other contributors.
   Licence:  MIT. Neither voxgig-attic/swim-js nor mrhooray/swim-js has a
             LICENSE file; the licence is declared only in their
             package.json ("license": "MIT"). lib/swim/LICENSE gives the MIT
             text with that author.

   Local changes:
   * codec.js: the native msgpack 1.0.3 module, which no longer builds on
     Node.js 24 or 26, is replaced by @msgpack/msgpack (pure JavaScript).
     Every mesh 2.x node uses this codec. The MessagePack format family is
     the same, but dates, objects with a toJSON method and functions are
     encoded differently, so mesh 2.x does not support mixed clusters with
     seneca-mesh 1.x nodes.
   * membership.js: the native farmhash module is replaced by a node:crypto
     (SHA-256) hash in checksum(). The checksum is local only; no message
     carries it.
   * net.js: the UDP socket is created in listen(). close() closes it and no
     longer creates a new socket, which kept a handle open after leave().
     Nothing is sent once the socket is closed.
   * swim.js: leave() also stops a join that is still waiting for an answer.
   * failure-detector.js: no ping is sent after stop().
   * new Buffer() is replaced by Buffer.alloc() and Buffer.from().
   * The debug module is replaced by util.debuglog (NODE_DEBUG=swim), and
     the clone module by lodash cloneDeep.
   * Each file has a header comment that names its origin.


2. sneeze (lib/sneeze.js)

   Origin:   sneeze 3.0.0
             https://github.com/rjrodger/sneeze
             commit 2dc3f49db92eaafaa1175b4deebdd3dd2a704a5f (tag v3.0.0),
             identical to the npm tarball of sneeze 3.0.0.
   Files:    sneeze.js of that commit, copied to lib/sneeze.js.
   Author:   Richard Rodger and other contributors.
   Licence:  MIT, Copyright (c) 2016 Richard Rodger. The licence text is in
             lib/sneeze.LICENSE, unchanged.

   Local changes:
   * Uses the vendored swim in lib/swim/ instead of @voxgig/swim.
   * The terminal monitor (make_monitor, parse_meta) and its option
     monitor are removed, with the modules keypress, ansi-escapes, pad,
     chalk and jsonpath that only it used.
   * Optioner/Joi option checking is replaced by plain defaults with the
     same rules: a key that is undefined takes its default, an array
     replaces the default array, and other keys pass through. silent must
     be a boolean and bases an array.
   * A node whose join fails leaves its swim instance before it retries or
     gives up, and leave() leaves every swim instance of the node (also when
     join() was called more than once) and cancels pending join retries, so
     that no socket or timer stays open. The join callbacks act on their
     own swim instance.
   * The default identifier uses the constant version 3.0.0 instead of
     reading the version from sneeze's package.json.


The tests of both packages are vendored too, moved to node:test:
test/swim/*.test.js from test/*.js of swim-js (tape), and test/sneeze.test.js
from test/sneeze.test.js of sneeze (lab).
